Version 0.1.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-09-06

Notes:
 * First tagged release. Mail can be read, written and sent, but this is
   still an early version: keep a second mail program for anything that
   matters.

Features:
 * IMAP accounts with a setup assistant that finds the server settings for
   most providers; passwords are kept in the system keyring.
 * Mail is synchronised for offline reading, with new messages arriving as
   the server announces them.
 * Writing and sending, with formatted text, attachments and inline
   images. A message that cannot be sent right away waits in the outbox
   and is retried; a copy is filed in Sent.
 * Microsoft 365 and Outlook.com accounts through GNOME Online Accounts,
   with no separate sign-in.
 * HTML mail is cleaned before it is shown, and remote images stay blocked
   until you ask for them or trust the sender. Attached messages open in a
   window of their own.
 * Attachments can be opened, saved one by one or saved all at once.
 * The message list can be narrowed to unread or flagged messages.
 * The folder sidebar can be folded, and folders pinned to Favourites.
 * Recipients are completed from the system address books and from the
   people you have written to before.
 * Czech translation.

Notes:
 * Search and conversation threading are not available yet.
 * Gmail accounts are not supported yet.
